u} be the statistics for the reconstructed image. 3. Local Distortion Calculation: Compute the local Wasserstein distortion d{	ext{WD}} at (x, y) using the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) between the local statistics: d{	ext{WD}}(x, y) = \sqrt {(\mu - \hat {\mu })^2 + (
u - \hat {
u })^2} This is equivalent to computing the squared 2-Wasserstein divergence W2^2 between two 1D Gaussian distributions defined by (\mu, 
u) and (\hat{\mu}, \hat{
u}). 4. Aggregation: Spatially average and sum the local d{	ext{WD}} values across all spatial locations and all feature maps to produce the final metric. Pseudocode: Unverified code. The code below did not pass a test run against a reference implementation, or no test fits it, so it may contain errors. import torch import torch.nn.functional as F def wassersteindistortion(featuresgt, featurespred, sigma=4): """ Computes Wasserstein Distortion between ground truth and predicted feature maps. Args: featuresgt: List of tensors [F1, F2,...], ground truth VGG features of shape (B, C, H, W). featurespred: List of tensors [F1, F2,...], predicted VGG features of shape (B, C, H, W). sigma: Hyperparameter for kernel size. Note: sources define kernel size as either sigma or 2sigma. Returns: Scalar tensor representing the WD score. """ # VGG feature extraction is external to this metric. totaldistortion = 0.0 # Using 2sigma as per; adjust to sigma if following kernelsize = 2 sigma padding = kernelsize // 2 for Fgt, Fpred in zip(featuresgt, featurespred): # Step 2: Local Statistics Computation # Compute local mean meangt = F.avgpool2d(Fgt, kernelsize=kernelsize, stride=1, padding=padding) meanpred = F.avgpool2d(Fpred, kernelsize=kernelsize, stride=1, padding=padding) # Compute local standard deviation: sqrt(E[X^2] - (E[X])^2) sqgt = F.avgpool2d(Fgt 2, kernelsize=kernelsize, stride=1, padding=padding) sqpred = F.avgpool2d(Fpred 2, kernelsize=kernelsize, stride=1, padding=padding) # Clamp variance to non-negative values for numerical stability vargt = torch.clamp(sqgt - meangt 2, min=0.0) varpred = torch.clamp(sqpred - meanpred 2, min=0.0) stdgt = torch.sqrt(vargt) stdpred = torch.sqrt(varpred) # Step 3: Local Distortion Calculation # dWD = sqrt( (mu - muhat)^2 + (nu - nuhat)^2) localdistortion = torch.sqrt((meangt - meanpred) 2 + (stdgt - stdpred) 2) # Step 4: Aggregation # Spatially average over H and W, then sum across channels (feature maps) totaldistortion += localdistortion